---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro'

const effectiveDate = 'October 4, 2026'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy & Facility Data Responsibilities"
  description="Privacy controls, facility deployment responsibilities, and agreements required before using ShorelineOps with resident information."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <div class="marketing-document relative py-16 sm:py-24 overflow-hidden">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <!-- Header -->
      <div class="mb-10 text-center sm:text-left">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/60 border border-emerald-200 dark:border-emerald-800/80 text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-300 text-xs font-mono font-semibold mb-4">
          <Icon name="shield-check" class="w-3.5 h-3.5" />
          <span>PRIVACY & PHI RESPONSIBILITIES</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-3">
          Privacy & Facility Data Responsibilities
        </h1>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          Updated: {effectiveDate} · Deployment guidance; not an executed privacy agreement or BAA
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Trust Badges Frosted Card -->
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white/70 dark:bg-slate-900/60 backdrop-blur-xl border border-slate-200/80 dark:border-slate-800/80 shadow-sm mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xs font-bold font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mb-4">Patient Health Information Safeguards</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-xs">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
            <Icon name="lock" class="w-4 h-4 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" />
            <div>
              <div class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Hosting safeguards</div>
              <p class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-0.5">Verify TLS, database encryption, backup encryption, and key custody in the selected deployment.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
            <Icon name="clipboard-check" class="w-4 h-4 text-shoreline-600 dark:text-shoreline-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" />
            <div>
              <div class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Decision audit records</div>
              <p class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-0.5">Protected decisions record the authenticated actor. Retention and tamper resistance require deployment validation.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
            <Icon name="shield-check" class="w-4 h-4 text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" />
            <div>
              <div class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Resident data boundaries</div>
              <p class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-0.5">Do not send resident records to public demos, SDK labs, advertising services, or unapproved AI providers.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Policy Body -->
      <div class="space-y-10 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        <!-- Section 1 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">01.</span>
            Scope & Deployment Review
          </h2>
          <p>This page describes current product boundaries and responsibilities for facilities considering ShorelineOps. It does not establish a legal entity, execute a Business Associate Agreement (BAA), or certify HIPAA compliance.</p>
          <p>Before processing resident information, identify the contracting parties, permitted uses, hosting providers, and applicable agreements with the facility and qualified privacy counsel.</p>

        </section>

        <!-- Section 2 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">02.</span>
            Resident Information Boundaries
          </h2>
          <p>Resident records support dietary operations, clinical review, and tray verification. Use only information necessary for approved workflows and limit access to authorized staff.</p>
          <p>Public demos use synthetic information. The isolated Muse SDK laboratory has no resident-record or database connection. Any future AI or device integration requires a separately reviewed data boundary before facility use.</p>

        </section>

        <!-- Section 3 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">03.</span>
            Technical Safeguards & Architecture
          </h2>
          <p>Clinical operations require one facility per deployment and database. Shared multi-facility clinical isolation is not established.</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2"><li>Server-side permissions restrict protected actions, including clinical reconciliation and purchasing approval.</li>
            <li>Authentication uses bcrypt password hashing and signed access tokens. Configure session expiry and available multi-factor authentication for shared devices.</li>
            <li>Validate HTTPS, encryption at rest, backup security, access policies, audit retention, and incident response in the actual deployment.</li></ul>
          <p>These controls support privacy procedures; source inspection alone does not prove regulatory compliance.</p>

        </section>

        <!-- Section 4 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">04.</span>
            Agreements Required Before Rollout
          </h2>
          <p>A facility handling PHI must establish applicable business associate and subcontractor agreements before rollout. Executed agreements should define permitted processing, incident reporting, access requests, retention, termination, and secure disposal responsibilities.</p>
          <p>No breach-notification deadline or data-destruction guarantee is created by this informational page.</p>

        </section>

        <!-- Section 5 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">05.</span>
            Facility BAA Review
          </h2>
          <p>Confirm the availability and terms of a facility-specific BAA with the contracting parties before entering PHI. Automated BAA onboarding and a downloadable signed agreement are not currently represented as available product features.</p>
          <p>Review <a href="/security" class="underline text-shoreline-600 dark:text-shoreline-400">security and deployment responsibilities</a> alongside your hosting arrangements and facility procedures.</p>

        </section>

        <!-- Section 6 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">06.</span>
            Reporting & Facility Contacts
          </h2>
          <p>Use the security reporting instructions in the <a href="https://github.com/ShadowWalkerNC/ShorelineOps/blob/main/SECURITY.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="underline text-shoreline-600 dark:text-shoreline-400">project security policy</a> for suspected vulnerabilities. Do not include resident records or credentials in public issues.</p>
          <p>Facility privacy requests and legal notices must use contacts established in the applicable executed service agreement.</p>

        </section>
      </div>

      <!-- Action Navigation -->
      <div class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 flex flex-wrap gap-4 justify-between items-center text-xs">
        <a href="/terms" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-shoreline-600 dark:text-shoreline-400 hover:underline font-semibold">
          <span>View Service & Licensing Information</span>
          <Icon name="arrow-right" class="w-3.5 h-3.5" />
        </a>
        <a href="/security" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 hover:text-slate-900 dark:hover:text-white">
          <span>Explore Technical Security Architecture</span>
          <Icon name="arrow-right" class="w-3.5 h-3.5" />
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
